new file mode 100644
index 0000000..280d8e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FIXES-0.2.12.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Concat 0.2.12 — Auto Captions fixes
+
+This source tree contains three targeted changes to the 0.2.12 source.
+
+## 1. Captions across split clips
+
+When the selected clip is one piece of a continuous split, Auto Captions now finds the complete adjacent source chain on that timeline track and sends the combined source range to Whisper. The chain must use the same media file, audio stream, and constant playback speed, with no gap or overlap in either timeline time or source time. Selecting either the head or tail finds the same chain. Unrelated uses of the same file are left alone. Clips with speed curves retain the previous single-clip behavior.
+
+## 2. Word range for generated speech captions
+
+The speech-captions form now has **Minimum words** and **Maximum words** controls (1–12). The defaults are 2 and 4, and the chosen values are saved in application preferences. Old settings files remain compatible and use those defaults.
+
+Whisper returns phrase-level timestamps, not word-level timestamps. When a phrase is split, its time is therefore apportioned between the resulting captions by the character count of each word group. Short neighboring phrases are merged when their gap is at most 0.6 seconds and the merged caption remains within the selected maximum. A very short isolated phrase may still fall below the minimum rather than joining across a long pause; the maximum is respected.
+
+## 3. Long silence between speech captions
+
+When Whisper returns one caption spanning multiple speech regions that Silero VAD separated in the original audio, the caption is now split across those speech regions. Words are assigned to the separate regions in proportion to their detected speech duration. Each resulting caption is bounded by its own speech region, so a long interval between regions (for example, 20 seconds) is left without a subtitle. If VAD has no matching region or its result is not trusted, the previous Whisper timing fallback is retained.
+
+## Tests and validation
+
+New Rust unit tests cover word grouping, merging nearby short phrases, preserving a 20-second silence between two speech regions, preference serialization/backward compatibility, and finding split chains from either side while excluding speed/audio-stream mismatches.
+
+In the preparation environment, all locale JSON files parsed; the locale inventory reported no stale keys (new labels are translated in Arabic and fall back to English in other locales); the Slint-to-Rust callback paths were checked; and a word-partition model was exercised for ranges 1–12. A Rust toolchain (`rustc`, `cargo`, and `rustfmt`) was not available, so the Rust tests, Slint compilation, formatting check, and Windows executable build have **not** been run here.
+
+To build and test on a configured development machine, use the repository's documented toolchain (Rust 1.93 and native dependencies), then from `src/` run:
+
+```sh
+cargo test
+cargo build --profile app -p concat
+```
